definitive reasons if they are still debated. Stick to the consensus view (retention for respiratory control).\n\n5.  **Constructing the Final Answer:**\n    *   Start with the Endosymbiotic Theory.\n    *   Detail the genomic features supporting this (circularity, ribosomes, duplication).\n    *   Connect to macroevolution (simplifies cell complexity without building the organelle).\n    *   Mention the incomplete genome (secondary gene transfer).\n    *   Conclude on the significance: Vertical genealogy vs. Horizontal events.\n\n6.  **Applying Constraints:**\n    *   Native thinking check: Do I need to show work? No, just think through the argument silently before generating the text.\n    *   Format: Single block at the end `'}]}
